            0.112,
            0.108,
            0.885,
            0.166
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "value that we get “closer” and “closer” to as we add more and more terms of the infinite sum, starting from the first term. You will learn more about infinite series in higher grades."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.166,
            0.886,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the number line is not only filled with rational numbers but also contains irrational numbers. We have seen how to mark some irrationals, and will simply conceive the rest of the irrationals to lie on the line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.232,
            0.847,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
